        "original_id": "a3f547e7-840f-5c30-b158-a646ad68cb1c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Robert E. Howard\n- Products: Conan the Barbarian, pulp magazines\n- Concepts: pulp fiction, fictional worlds\n- Topics: magazine publishing formats\n\nFacts:\n- Pulp magazines were inexpensive fiction magazines that were published from 1896 to the 1950s.\n- Robert E. Howard was a pulp fiction writer of the 1930s.\n- Robert E. Howard wrote stories about Conan the Barbarian, an eponymous character whose adventures take place in a fictional pre-historic world of dark magic and savagery.\n- The 1982 film Conan the Barbarian is based on stories by Robert E. Howard.\n- A typical pulp magazine had 128 pages and measured 7 inches wide, 10 inches high, and 0.5 inch thick, with ragged, untrimmed edges.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
