        "original_id": "9f881674-1f09-55a2-85d6-313687181c62",
        "text": "Page: Conan the Barbarian (1982 film). Sentence: It is based on stories by Robert E. Howard, a pulp fiction writer of the 1930s, about the adventures of the eponymous character in a fictional pre-historic world of dark magic and savagery.\nPage: Pulp magazine. Sentence: Pulp magazines or Pulp Fiction (often referred to as \"the pulps\") were inexpensive fiction magazines that were published from 1896 to the 1950s.\nPage: Pulp magazine. Sentence: The typical pulp magazine had 128 pages; it was 7 in wide by 10 in high, and 0.5 inch thick, with ragged, untrimmed edges.",
